Subject: [PATCH 62/88] xhttp: no post interval for a range from zero; tests
 for rotation and deadlines

A range of sc_min_posts_interval_ms that starts at zero means no waiting
between posts, as with Xray; a wait was drawn from it. Tests: a pooled
connection past h_max_reusable_secs takes no new sessions and keeps its own;
deadlines report that they are not supported.
---
 transport/v2rayxhttp/conn.go        |  4 ++
 transport/v2rayxhttp/review_test.go | 61 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 transport/v2rayxhttp/upload.go      |  3 +-
 3 files changed, 67 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/transport/v2rayxhttp/conn.go b/transport/v2rayxhttp/conn.go
